{#
  The post a reply answers, cited in the reply (TASK-123): an embedded
  `u-in-reply-to h-cite` that always carries the target's URL, so a parser
  reads what this post answers even when nothing more is known about it.

  Drawn as the citation block (doc-9): a rule on the start side, a sans line
  naming the target, and its words as an italic quote. An entry includes it
  with `inReplyTo` and `replyContext` on the context; a feed sets both from
  the entry it is printing.

  `replyContext` is what the target said about itself when the reply was saved
  or synced: its name, a short excerpt, its author and its date, each only when
  it said so. It is somebody else's words, so every piece is printed through
  autoescaping and none of it with `safe`. With a name, the name is the link;
  with only an author, "a post" is; with neither, "a page on" its host. Its date is
  written in `lang`, the language of the entry it sits in (TASK-189), so a
  listing sets `lang` from each entry as it sets `replyContext`.

  `replyContext.picture`, when the target has one and the reply shows it, is
  drawn as a thumbnail beside the line, as `citations.njk` draws it (TASK-252).

  `replyContext.original`, when the target is a silo copy of a post that lists
  the copy as its own (TASK-197), is the post cited: the `h-cite` links the
  original and describes it, so its site finds the link when it is sent a
  webmention. The copy follows the citation as a `u-in-reply-to` of its own,
  outside the `h-cite`, so the silo can thread the reply too.
#}
{% import "partials/cited-page.njk" as cited %}
{% if inReplyTo %}
{% set picture = replyContext.picture %}
{% set answered = replyContext.original or inReplyTo %}
<div class="reply-context cite u-in-reply-to h-cite{% if picture %} cite-with-thumb{% endif %}">
  {%- if picture %}{{ cited.thumb(answered, picture) }}{% endif %}
  <p class="cite-line small">In reply to
    {{- cited.page(answered, replyContext) }}
    {%- if replyContext.published %}, <time class="dt-published" datetime="{{ replyContext.published | date("iso") }}">{{ replyContext.published | date("readable", none, lang) }}</time>
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>
  {% if replyContext.text %}
  <blockquote class="cite-quote p-content">{{ replyContext.text }}</blockquote>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% if replyContext.original %}
<p class="cite-copy small">Also in reply to <a class="u-in-reply-to" href="{{ inReplyTo }}">its copy on {{ inReplyTo | host }}</a></p>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
